 "overview": {
  "summary": "The board every output in the instrument passes through on its way to the binding posts. Thirty-three latching two- and four-pole relays, driven by eight UCN5801 latching drivers (U5-U12) under an 82C55 (U1), route the DAC, the Oscillator, the Power Amplifier and the High Voltage assemblies to OUTPUT HI, OUTPUT LO, SENSE HI and SENSE LO, and switch the analog and digital commons for operate, standby and calibration. A ninth UCN5801 (U13) drives the ten non-latching relays on the Analog Motherboard from a local 3.5 V/7 V supply (U17, Q1, Q2) so that those coils run cool and contribute no thermal EMF. Three analog blocks sit alongside the switching. The dc 2.2 V range is made here: the 5700A-4HR1 heated hybrid and its bonded resistor network divide the DAC's 11 V range by five and buffer it, and a CA3096 array (U19) with Q4 turns that into a 50 mA output stage. The same network carries the 10:1 and 100:1 dividers that make the ac and dc 220 mV, 22 mV and 2.2 mV ranges, all at 50 ohm output impedance. And the internal cal zero amplifier (U20, U21, Z2) removes the offset of every dc range except 1100 V, comparing each in turn against R COM through FET Q7 at a gain of 10 or 130 and reporting to the adc on A11 over RCL. A 4051 multiplexer (U4) reads eight diagnostic channels onto SDL, which makes A8 the measuring path for the guarded supply rails of the whole analog section.",
  "sections": "§2-87 … §2-99",
  "note": "A8 generates no supply of its own. Nine rails arrive from A17 on P202 — +8 RLH, +5 RLH and RLH COM for the relay drivers, +5 LH, LH COM and -5 LH for the digital section, and +17 S, S COM and -17 S for the analog — each through a 6-turn choke (L1-L4). The three commons are not interchangeable: RLH COM belongs to the relay coils, LH COM to the guarded digital bus, and S COM (TP9) to the analog supplies, while R COM (TP8) is the precision common that U21's current-cancellation circuit keeps current out of. §5-9 uses three different references in six steps, and one of them is the front panel OUTPUT LO binding post rather than anything on the board."
 },
