   "mfrCode": "89536",
   "mfrPart": "813436",
   "function": "The 5700A-4HR1 heated hybrid: a precision dc amplifier die (marked AD707C on schematic sheet 3, with 300/300 input resistors, 25K/25K feedback and 6.2 V clamps) held at 50 °C by a heater control block drawn sealed inside the HR1 HYBRID outline. It buffers the divided DAC voltage that becomes the dc 2.2 V range, and its OVEN TEMP output is what fault code 3824 measures. Filed here as 'mech' because the parts list gives it an H designator; it is nothing of the kind. Note the naming: the 1996 list calls it H2, the Rev 9 list HY1, the board silkscreen HR1 and the schematic all three — see the caveats.",
